  "title": "SGLang manager completion signals retain distinct success and ownership conditions",
  "mechanism": "At the pinned SGLang revision, HostCopyDone.query reports completion even when a copy failed; synchronize waits and rethrows a stored error. The copy worker signals completion in finally after waiting for the producer event and using its private stream, while shutdown only joins for the requested timeout without a post-join liveness check. FanOutCommunicator queueing calls share an untagged event and result list, clear them only after the wait returns, and count received responses against fan_out. Cancellation of a waiter does not itself correlate late responses or clear this shared state. HiCache _page_transfer continues producing one PrefetchAck per storage batch after cooperative termination or a failed batch; the consumer MIN-reduces completed token counts across completion groups. DPBudget speculatively increments requests and estimated input tokens; refresh is throttled to 20 ms and total_tokens_scheduler charges len(input_ids). This is a dispatch heuristic, not an observed completion cost. Follow-bootstrap routing takes bootstrap_room modulo the entire worker list without checking active status at that point; elastic activation asserts that its socket was already bound, so an inactive slot does not necessarily mean a None socket.",
  "corrections": [
    "Completion is not copy success; destination validity requires the error-bearing synchronization path.",
    "Untagged shared communicator state does not prove that an actual race occurred in a running service.",
    "Preserve the per-batch acknowledgement cadence even when no further storage copy succeeds.",
    "Replace the candidate's inactive-slot-implies-None claim with the narrower missing active-status guard.",
    "No throughput, latency improvement, hardware behavior or complete scheduler cancellation protocol was measured."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
